 ## Divergences
 
-- **Where macros may be registered (DIV-11.2).** Macros live in the Scope Frame, never in a module variable or a static field (AD-5). Registering one is a base-only write: `macro`, `mixin` and `flushMacros` pass only when the innermost frame is a `test` frame, and throw `ScopeFrameException` in every other frame (a `request`, `job`, `command` or `unit` frame, and a unit or narrow frame nested in a test frame) and with no active frame (ESC-11.1-5, ESC-11.1-6). Inside a test frame the macros apply to that test only and are discarded when it ends, so a Ported Test that registers macros in its body keeps doing so.
